---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/blog/what-is-epr/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />
  <h1>What Is EPR?</h1>
  <p class="lede">EPR (Extended Producer Responsibility) is a regulatory principle requiring manufacturers of electrical and electronic equipment to take responsibility for the collection, recycling, and environmentally sound disposal of their products at end-of-life. In India, EPR is embedded in the E-Waste (Management) Rules 2022.</p>

  <CtaBar whatsappMessage="Hi, I have a question about What Is EPR?." />

  <ul class="key-takeaways">
    <li>Under EPR, producers must establish collection systems, achieve annual recycling targets, and fund the end-to-end management of their sold products.</li>
    <li>EPR ensures that brands finance the reverse logistics and recycling of the products they sell.</li>
    <li>Producers register with CPCB, file annual returns, and maintain records of collection, dismantling, and recycling.</li>
  </ul>

  <section>
    <h2>How EPR Works</h2>
    <p>Under EPR, producers must establish collection systems, achieve annual recycling targets, and fund the end-to-end management of their sold products. They may fulfill these obligations directly or through authorized Producer Responsibility Organizations (PROs).</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Impact on Consumers</h2>
    <p>EPR ensures that brands finance the reverse logistics and recycling of the products they sell. Consumers benefit through free or low-cost collection channels, formal recycling channels, and reduced environmental harm from unregulated disposal.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Compliance Pathway</h2>
    <p>Producers register with CPCB, file annual returns, and maintain records of collection, dismantling, and recycling. Non-compliance attracts penalties and potential suspension of authorization under the Rules.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <details>
  <summary>Does EPR mean free pickup for consumers?</summary>
  <p>EPR obliges producers to fund collection infrastructure. Many authorized recyclers offer free doorstep pickup as part of fulfilling producer obligations.</p>
</details>
  <details>
  <summary>Who enforces EPR?</summary>
  <p>CPCB and State PCBs enforce EPR obligations under E-Waste Rules 2022.</p>
</details>
  <details>
  <summary>What is a PRO?</summary>
  <p>A Producer Responsibility Organization is an authorized entity that helps producers meet their EPR targets on their behalf.</p>
</details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Related Resources</h2>
